p=neural['primary'];write('RUHI-V6-NEURAL-BENCHMARK.md',intro+'## CPU-only evaluation\n\nNo model fitting, calibration changes, threshold tuning or promotion occurred. All six published artifacts are unchanged. The 408 context rows expand 68 new phrase forms across six vocabularies: 17 intent families and four meaning classes. They have zero exact phrase overlap with the saved Phase2 candidate corpus; semantic/template overlap and complete historical production-training provenance cannot be excluded.\n\n| Model | Joint context accuracy | Intent macro F1 | Intent ECE | Accepted correct/accepted |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'+'\n'.join(lines)+f"\n\nPublished primary: 102 deduplicated phrases from seven authored numeric command families, fixed graph2d mode. Action {100*p['action']['accuracy']:.2f}%, sub-action {100*p['subAction']['accuracy']:.2f}%, mode {100*p['mode']['accuracy']:.2f}%, object type {100*p['objectType']['accuracy']:.2f}%, all four heads {100*p['semanticExactMatch']:.2f}%. Full confusion matrices, class support/precision/recall/F1, calibration bins and latency are in neural-evaluation.json. Known/common command templates are diagnostic evidence, not guaranteed unseen primary training holdout.\n\n## Comparisons and promotion decision\n\nPhase2 candidate synthetic locked result was 942/1088 (86.58%); published context was 335/1088 (30.79%). This new corpus differs, so 195/408 versus 188/408 is a new stress measurement, not a controlled before/after accuracy improvement. Selective candidate accuracy is 19/21 (90.48%) at only 5.15% coverage; it falls below the historical calibration target. Candidate **NOT PROMOTED**. Human-authored held-out language and broader meanings remain blocked.\n\nNode tensor count returns from 0 to 0 after disposal. Browser candidate CPU100 median 0.4ms, p95 0.7ms, tensors 24→30→24; memory estimates are explicitly unreliable.\n"+repro)
write('RUHI-V6-MATH-VERIFICATION-REPORT.md',intro+'## Covered independent evidence\n\nNumeric fixtures use direct arithmetic, midpoint, slope, centroid, area/volume and coordinate invariants. Exact rational/polynomial checks retain independent symbolic evidence; float geometry uses numerical_consistency. Deliberately wrong derivative, expansion and equivalence certificates are contradicted. False area assertions and nonparallel lines do not become verified. The new tangent checker tests actual finite 2D center-to-line distance against radius, rejects a shifted tangent, and gives a Euclidean explanation without claiming universal symbolic proof.\n\nImpossible SSS, zero/negative dimensions, degenerate vertex edits, missing references and malformed imports reject or ask for defined data before committed effects. Symbolic vertex edits preserve parent identity and update medians/centroid; native two-workspace checks pass.\n\n## Before/after\n\nNonlocked fixture agreement improved from 7919/8677 to 8677/8677; final10000/10000. Scoped7864, frozen100 and final-focused30 pass. These are fixture agreement counts, not a proof that all outputs are mathematically verified. Advanced CAS/domain conditions, universal proofs and unrestricted comparison remain bounded or valid_unverified.\n\n## Legacy oracle conflicts\n\nFour original NLP300 fixtures ask to move C while the scene has only P1. Earlier fallback moved that unrelated point. The current engine returns invalid without geometry mutation. The original benchmark stays **failed**, and complete conflicts are preserved in legacy-oracle-conflicts.json. A new focused test asserts the safe rejection. Three regular-trapezoid cases remain blocked because they are underdefined.\n')
write('RUHI-V6-CONVERSATION-RELIABILITY.md',intro+'## Covered working memory\n\nTests cover 2,5,10,20,50,100 alternating edit/query turns, exact evolving width/area, stable identity, undo/redo, ordinal disambiguation, line point→angle clarification and relative angle continuation. Conversation text caps at25 turns; undo caps at100; the current construction and named object IDs persist. Import clears transient conversational state and validates history before effects.\n\nMissing distance in Move rectangle R1 right asks a question; R1 is not reinterpreted as radius1. Supplied distance resumes the pending move. Nonexistent C does not move P1. Vertex C edits a real triangle parent and its dependents; a collinear edit is rejected atomically.\n\nExisting Phase2 isolation, alias/style persistence, stale pending reference and cancellation tests remain in the passed scoped suite. Final-focused30 and isolated legacy23 pass. This is bounded working memory, not an unlimited transcript-recall or every tutoring-domain guarantee.\n')
registry=Path('src/math-robo/intelligence/studioCapabilities.ts').read_text();write('RUHI-V6-CROSS-STUDIO-REPORT.md',intro+'## Actual routes and native validation\n\nThe typed studioCapabilities registry lists 11 existing routes: Unit Circle, algebra, geometry, calculus, differential equations, number systems, probability, 2D/3D graphs and 2D/3D geometry workspaces. Open requests produce a bounded route proposal; ambiguous graph requests ask for2D/3D; unknown studios are unsupported. Populated scenes require an explicit Confirm opening action.\n\n38 native normal-entry checks pass across graph2d, geometry2d, graph3d, geometry3d, including physical dimension edits, compound planning, tutoring, ambiguity, undo and dependent construction updates. The built student UI preserves the populated scene until confirmation and opens the actual Unit Circle route offline.\n\n## Incomplete breadth\n\nNot every registered route has a native mathematical acceptance matrix. Linear algebra, complex numbers, discrete/graph-theory, statistics and modelling already have app modules, but their full conversational EXPLAIN/PROVE/VISUALIZE/VERIFY/MODIFY/COMPARE/TUTOR matrix was not completed here. Navigation itself does not establish grounded domain competence. Unsupported requests retain explicit limits. Gate G is BLOCKED.\n')
write('RUHI-V6-PERFORMANCE-REPORT.md',intro+f"## Measured desktop host\n\nFinal10000 complete semantic interactions: median {final['timing']['medianMs']:.3f}ms, p95 {final['timing']['p95Ms']:.3f}ms, maximum {final['timing']['maxMs']:.3f}ms. Baseline nonlocked median2.21ms/p954.825ms/max163.78ms; different sample counts and concurrent workloads prevent claiming a controlled speed improvement.\n\nBrowser candidate CPU100: median0.4ms/p950.7ms, 28026 parameters; tensors24→30→24. Node new context latency and all calibration/class metrics appear in neural-evaluation.json. Semantic corpus throughput is not cinematic rendering FPS or native end-to-end latency.\n\nOffline installer: {len(package['assets'])} assets, {package['bytes']} bytes ({package['bytes']/1024/1024:.2f}MiB), four concurrent fetch/hash jobs. Latest local installation {offline['installationMs']}ms. Bounds:4096 input characters,32 planned commands,1000 imported objects,4096 vertices/object,100 history entries,25 conversation turns,2000 offline assets/512MiB total/64MiB per asset.\n\n## Hardware limits\n\nThis host ran desktop/headless Chromium with software WebGL and explicit CPU model inference. No physical low-end Android/browser quota/mobile thermal or memory-pressure guarantee is established. No universal FPS or device-performance claim; low-end acceptance remains BLOCKED.\n")
write('RUHI-V6-SECURITY-AND-OFFLINE-AUDIT.md',intro+'## Installed student build\n\nLatest production-browser check: **11 passed,0 failed,0 errors**. A complete hash-verified installation is followed by network disconnection, fresh page navigation and reload in all four workspaces; local models load and creation, movement and measurement execute. Navigation confirmation and offline Unit Circle transition also pass. Development on9867 does not register this installer; production student builds do.\n\nVersion identity includes assets and unpatched worker source. Installation verifies every asset SHA-256 and size and writes its completion manifest last. A failure deletes only the incomplete version. Updates wait for existing clients to close, preserving current work; activation removes only older Ruhi caches. Preview Vary headers are removed/ignored for trusted hash-verified static assets. Three packaging checks verify idempotence, trainer exclusion and distinct cache versions on worker-only changes. Four worker tests verify integrity rejection/cleanup, foreign-origin rejection, activation scope and completion ordering.\n\n## Input and roles\n\nMalformed scene controls, object ID mismatches, nonfinite/disagreeing coordinates, dangling selected references, mode mismatch, oversized expression/history and executable plot text are rejected before effects. Existing request cancellation/stale result tests pass. Student bundle excludes datasets, reports, training worker and trainer entry; no six-model artifact changed. Client-side guards cannot authenticate against a device owner modifying JavaScript or storage. No secure cloud/production trainer authentication claim.\n\n## Limits\n\nOffline installation consumes approximately153MiB and can fail safely under quota/network limitations; no installed guarantee is presented until completion. Subpath deployment, arbitrary browser versions, physical mobile-device quota and full UI/theme/stress coverage remain incomplete.\n'+history)
write('RUHI-V6-RELEASE-GATES.md',intro+'| Gate | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join(f'| {g} — {n} | **{s}** | {e} |' for g,n,s,e in gates)+'\n\n`final-evidence.json` records seeds, source and artifact hashes, model integrity, tests, gates and command configuration. No failed original fixture was removed or reclassified as a pass.\n')
write('RUHI-V6-FINAL-REPORT.md',intro+'## Results\n\n- Adversarial corpus:10000 generated/validated/executed/passed;0 failed,44 grammar families. Controlled synthetic/state-expanded coverage.\n- Development/regression baseline:7919/8677→8677/8677 after758 fixture failures repaired.\n- Scoped tests:7864 passed/65files; final focused30 passed; legacy-output-isolation23 passed. Suites overlap.\n- Frozen conversations:100/100. Original NLP300:293 passed,4 failed missing-C oracle conflicts,3 blocked underdefined trapezoids.\n- Native workspaces:38/38. Installed-student cold-offline/UI checks:11/11. Packaging checks:3/3.\n'+f"- TypeScript:218→{static['typescriptErrors']}. ESLint:439→{static['eslintErrors']} errors;133→{static['eslintWarnings']} warnings. Student build succeeds; checked release fails.\n"+'- Published context188/408 versus candidate195/408 on new controlled stress rows; primary four-head exact20/102. No broad unseen-human accuracy claim and no model promotion.\n- Six published model artifacts unchanged. No commit/push/deploy/retrain/v7.\n\n## Fixed behavior\n\n'+'\n'.join('- '+x for x in fixes)+'\n\n## Unresolved blockers\n\nStatic diagnostics remain across lesson/adaptor/studio modules; they are preserved without suppressions. Neural historical provenance/human generalization, complete major-studio acceptance, low-end physical-device compatibility and full browser/theme/recovery breadth remain incomplete. The original NLP oracle conflicts stay visible. One historical Phase1 matrix report lost its original bytes during a legacy test and cannot be claimed preserved. The initial source was fingerprinted rather than fully archived before edits.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Production release BLOCKED.** This is a tested local Phase3 implementation and partial acceptance assessment, not completion of every capability in the master prompt or approval to ship. Gates B,K,L fail; F,G,I remain blocked. The code, original failures, limits and recovery incident are reviewable alongside machine-readable evidence.\n'+history+repro)
